# TASK-260830-2iint0 review verdict — changes requested

Reviewer run: RUN-260901-7bae7d (claude / opus-5, high)
Change Request: `CR-TASK-260830-2iint0-1` revision 1
Base OID `48db30b59e5e1bbc5e0cf73ec2e0e0eec3d215d1` -> candidate tree `6700b2d1012c83ec2b050002962c9855cb0aa807`

## Verdict

**changes_requested -> `to-dev`.**

The implementation is materially correct against the normative text and the
delivered evidence is far above positive-path-only. It is rejected on the
explicit Definition-of-Done evidence clauses, not on design: four production
refusal clauses can be individually narrowed with the suite staying green, the
registry-driven root gate is not proven per member, and the OS production entry
point named in the README is never driven.

## What was independently verified (not accepted on report)

Reviewed artifact identity confirmed first: every one of the 7 changed paths in
the working tree hashes identically to its blob in candidate tree
`6700b2d1012c83ec2b050002962c9855cb0aa807`, so all evidence below was gathered
against the exact reviewed revision.

Normative source re-fetched and pinned independently: `SPEC.md` at commit
`28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c` hashes to
`562546d240f0fa3e71b47e6359a002f9892c0efd97e19eb55917527552ac484a`, matching
`.spec/README.md` and `internal/specpin`. §3.2 and §6.1 were read from that
document, not from the producer's summary.

| Check | Command | Result |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Full suite | `go test ./... -count=1` | all 9 packages ok |
| Focused suite | `go test ./internal/config -count=1` | ok |
| Race | `go test ./internal/config -race -count=1` | ok |
| Coverage | `go test ./internal/config -cover` | 80.6% |
| Vet | `go vet ./...` | clean |
| Format | `gofmt -l internal/config internal/traceability` | clean |
| Cross-build | `GOOS=windows/linux GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | both ok |
| Traceability, assigned | `tracecheck -section 3.2 -section 6.1` | `assigned_scopes=2`, exit 0 |
| Traceability, repository | `tracecheck` | `contracts=60 normative_sections=36 acceptance_cases=30 fixtures=30`, exit 0 |

Normative conformance re-derived from §3.2 by hand: precedence (flag, non-empty
env, platform default), the exact five-row override registry and its flag/env
names, macOS / Linux / WSL2 / native-Windows default paths, the XDG inputs, the
"absolute before use" rule, and the "empty values are unset" rule all match the
specification tables. §6.1's `config.toml` selection leaf matches.

Two anti-self-mint controls were attacked and both hold:

- Renaming `TestLoadRefusesWrongOrUnreadableRootKinds` in `loader_test.go` makes
  the gate fail with *declaration ... is absent from ...*. The `AC-PATH-001`
  ownership rows are real bindings, not decoration.
- Appending a fabricated `section:6.3 -> Load` binding to
  `ownership.v0.5.0.json` fails on the reviewed projection digest. Ownership
  cannot be self-minted without an explicit review of the pin.

Secret-passthrough claim independently confirmed: `internal/config` contains no
`os.Environ`/`os.Getenv` call, the resolver looks up exactly the five documented
`AX_*` names plus the XDG/`APPDATA`/`LOCALAPPDATA` platform-default inputs, and
`Error.Error()` never carries a resolved value.

## Reviewer mutation campaign

35 mutants beyond the producer's 14, deliberately weighted toward **narrowing**
rather than deletion, run against `go test ./internal/config -count=1` in an
isolated copy under `.temp/TASK-260830-2iint0/review/tree`. 27 killed, 8
survived.

Killed (representative): flag-before-env precedence inversion; empty-env-as-set;
stat failure collapsed into absence; read failure collapsed into absence; root
stat failure collapsed into absence; unknown-override-class check narrowed to a
single literal; Linux `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` fail-closed narrowed to a `TempDir`
fallback; Windows `APPDATA`/`LOCALAPPDATA` fail-closed narrowed to fallbacks;
registry row dropped; an undocumented sixth `AX_CREDENTIAL_DIR` row added; an
extra ambient `AX_PROVIDER_TOKEN` lookup added; an unknown `AX_*` name
interpreted as an override; relative value not made absolute; macOS state leaf
drift; Linux `ax` leaf dropped; WSL2 routed to the macOS layout; provenance
forced to `platform-default`; snapshot document and path aliasing; invalid
platform accepted; error string echoing a machine-local path;
`validateRootKinds` removed entirely.

## Findings

### 1. Root kind/inspection enforcement is not proven per registry member (blocking)

`validateRootKinds` (`internal/config/loader.go:232`) iterates the five-row
registry and enforces directory kind for four classes, but the evidence pins
only two of them.

Failure scenario: narrow the loop skip from
`if specification.Class == ConfigFile` to
`if specification.Class == ConfigFile || specification.Class == CacheRoot` — or
the same for `RuntimeRoot` — and `go test ./internal/config -count=1` stays
**green**. A cache or runtime root that is an existing regular file, or whose
`stat` fails with `EACCES`, is then silently admitted as a valid root by the
production `Load` entry.

`TestLoadRefusesWrongOrUnreadableRootKinds` exercises `data-root` (wrong kind)
and `state-root` (stat failure) as hand-picked instances. The DoD requires
completeness here to be a derived property: the test must iterate
`OverrideRegistry()` and assert that **every** non-`config-file` member both
refuses a wrong kind and refuses an unreadable root, so that dropping any member
from enforcement reddens the suite.

### 2. The config-file regular-kind gate is pinned only against a directory (blocking)

`internal/config/loader.go:208` refuses a non-regular selected config file.

Failure scenario: narrow `if !info.Mode().IsRegular()` to
`if info.Mode().IsDir()` and the suite stays **green**. Every other non-regular
kind is then admitted and read: a FIFO selected via `--config`/`AX_CONFIG` makes
`Load` block indefinitely on `ReadFile`, and a character/block device makes it
read unbounded bytes into the returned document. §3.2 declares the value kind as
"Existing regular file", not "not a directory".

The root cause is the harness, not the assertion: `fakeFileSystem.Stat` can only
return a regular file or `fs.ModeDir`, so the gate is exercised over a
two-element domain. Extend the fake to synthesize `fs.ModeNamedPipe`,
`fs.ModeSocket`, `fs.ModeDevice`, and `fs.ModeSymlink` modes and assert
`ErrConfigNotRegular` for each.

### 3. `LoadOS`/`OSInputs` — the real OS entry point — have 0% coverage (blocking)

`go tool cover -func` reports `OSInputs` 0.0% and `LoadOS` 0.0%. The README
names `LoadOS` as the production entry ("LoadOS captures the caller-supplied
runtime-probed AX platform and current OS inputs once"), and `internal/config`
has no external caller anywhere in the repository, so `LoadOS` *is* the
production call site for this slice and nothing drives it.

`OSInputs` additionally contains an untested refusal clause: the
`scalar.ParsePlatform` guard returning `ErrInvalidContext`. A gate that no test
executes has never run.

This is testable deterministically and without ambient dependence:
`LoadOS(scalar.Platform("solaris"), nil)` must return `ErrInvalidContext`
without touching the filesystem, and a positive case can set all five `AX_*`
variables with `t.Setenv` against `t.TempDir()` so no platform default and no
developer-machine state is consulted.

### 4. §3.2's "not-yet-created regular-file path whose parent exists" is unimplemented (blocking)

§3.2 gives the configuration file two admissible value kinds: an existing
regular file, **or** a not-yet-created regular-file path whose parent exists.
§6.1 makes normative defaults precedence layer 4, so a host with no
`config.toml` is ordinary operation, not an error.

`Load` implements only the first kind. On a fresh machine it returns
`ErrConfigNotFound` **and a zero `Snapshot`**, so the caller loses the resolved
root snapshot entirely on the most common startup path. The "parent exists"
branch is not validated anywhere and has no distinct outcome. The only evidence
for this case, `TestLoadDistinguishesAbsenceFromReadFailureAndWrongKind/absent
selected file`, asserts that absence is a failure.

`ResolvePaths` is exported and can be composed by a caller, but no production
path does so, and the README's "A missing config, wrong file kind, read failure,
and root inspection failure remain distinct" documents the sentinel without
resolving the contract question. Either implement the not-yet-created branch
(parent-exists validation, resolved snapshot returned, empty document) or state
explicitly in the README which task owns it and why absence is fatal here.

### 5. Three further refusal clauses survive individual narrowing (fix with the above)

Each of these is a clause the production code enforces today that no test pins,
so a future edit removes it silently:

- **Empty flag value as unset** (`selectCandidate`, `loader.go:309`). Changing
  `if value := overrides[class]; value != ""` to `if value, ok := ...; ok`
  leaves the suite green. §3.2's empty-value rule applies to the whole
  flag/environment registry; add an `Overrides{ConfigFile: ""}` case asserting
  the platform default with `SourcePlatformDefault` provenance.
- **Windows `..`-above-root refusal** (`cleanWindowsAbsolute`, `loader.go:538`).
  Replacing `return "", ErrInvalidContext` with `continue` leaves the suite
  green, converting an explicit refusal into silent truncation. Add
  `Overrides{DataRoot: "..\\..\\escape"}` against `C:\work` asserting
  `ErrInvalidContext`.
- **`Load` nil `Stat`/`ReadFile` guard** (`loader.go:179`). Removing it leaves
  the suite green and converts the refusal into a nil-func panic inside
  `validateRootKinds`. Add a `Load` call with an `Inputs` lacking the injected
  filesystem asserting `ErrInvalidContext`.

Two further survivors are noted as low severity and need no rework:
`OverrideRegistry` returning a non-isolated slice, and `absoluteWindowsPath`
rejecting forward-slash candidates (a fail-closed choice the specification does
not mandate either way).

### 6. `section:6.1` is claimed as sole owner while two of its MUSTs are unimplemented (address before the sibling task)

`ownership.v0.5.0.json` registers
`section:6.1 -> internal/config/loader.go:Load` as an implementation owner, and
`tracecheck -section 6.1` reports `assigned_scopes=1`. §6.1 also states
"Unknown top-level keys MUST fail configuration loading" and "Secret values MUST
NOT be accepted in config fields"; neither exists in this slice, and the README
correctly defers both to the versioned-schema task.

`internal/traceability/traceability.go:400` rejects a second owner for the same
key with *duplicate section_binding implementation owner*, so blocked-by sibling
`TASK-260830-17suox` cannot register its own `section:6.1` binding when it
implements those two refusals. Decide now whether §6.1 ownership should point at
the eventual decode entry, or whether the binding needs a sub-key, and record
the decision. As it stands the gate output overstates §6.1 coverage.

## Not findings

- Windows runtime default `%TEMP%\ax`: §3.2's Native Windows "Runtime IPC" cell
  describes pipes and handles rather than a path, while the prose requires a
  runtime root directory that `AX_RUNTIME_DIR` overrides. A default had to be
  chosen; the README makes no normativity claim about it.
- Hand-listed five-row registry in
  `TestOverrideRegistryIsExactAndDrivesEveryEnvironmentResolution`:
  `internal/specpin/v0.5.0.lock.json` does not pin the §3.2 override registry,
  so an independent second copy checked against the specification table is the
  only available derivation source and matches repository precedent.
- `TestLoadIsIdempotentReadOnlyAndReturnsIsolatedSnapshots` asserting
  `files.writeCount != 0`: vacuous, since `fakeFileSystem` has no write path and
  `Inputs` exposes no write capability. Harmless, but it proves nothing; the
  read-only property is enforced by the injected-dependency shape instead.
- 80.6% coverage is not itself a finding; finding 3 is about the entry point
  being undriven, not about the percentage.

## Rework routing

`to-dev`. Findings 1-4 must be closed with tests that redden under the exact
narrowing mutants named above; finding 5 should be closed in the same pass;
finding 6 needs a recorded decision. No specification conflict, platform
constraint, or human-only decision is involved, so this is ordinary rework, not
stop-the-line.

## Reviewer artifacts

- `TASK-260830-2iint0_reviewer-mutation-round1.log` — 22 mutants, delete + narrow
- `TASK-260830-2iint0_reviewer-mutation-round2.log` — 16 narrowing mutants
// Package config resolves the process-lifetime AX path snapshot and reads the
// selected configuration document. Versioned TOML decoding and migration are
// separate concerns; this package never mutates configuration or root state.
package config

import (
	"errors"
	"fmt"
	"io/fs"
	"os"
	"path"
	"strings"

	"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar"
)

var (
	ErrInvalidContext             = errors.New("invalid configuration loader context")
	ErrUnknownPathClass           = errors.New("unknown AX path class")
	ErrPlatformDefaultUnavailable = errors.New("platform path default unavailable")
	ErrConfigNotFound             = errors.New("selected configuration file not found")
	ErrConfigNotRegular           = errors.New("selected configuration path is not a regular file")
	ErrConfigRead                 = errors.New("configuration file read failed")
	ErrRootNotDirectory           = errors.New("selected root path is not a directory")
	ErrRootInspect                = errors.New("selected root path inspection failed")
)

// PathClass names one member of the complete AX 1.0.0 path override registry.
type PathClass string

const (
	ConfigFile  PathClass = "config-file"
	DataRoot    PathClass = "data-root"
	StateRoot   PathClass = "state-root"
	CacheRoot   PathClass = "cache-root"
	RuntimeRoot PathClass = "runtime-root"
)

// OverrideSpec binds one path class to its command flag and sole AX_*
// environment override. The registry is vocabulary, not a capability claim.
type OverrideSpec struct {
	Class       PathClass
	Flag        string
	Environment string
}

var overrideRegistry = [...]OverrideSpec{
	{Class: ConfigFile, Flag: "--config", Environment: "AX_CONFIG"},
	{Class: DataRoot, Flag: "--data-dir", Environment: "AX_DATA_DIR"},
	{Class: StateRoot, Flag: "--state-dir", Environment: "AX_STATE_DIR"},
	{Class: CacheRoot, Flag: "--cache-dir", Environment: "AX_CACHE_DIR"},
	{Class: RuntimeRoot, Flag: "--runtime-dir", Environment: "AX_RUNTIME_DIR"},
}

// OverrideRegistry returns an isolated ordered copy of the complete registry.
func OverrideRegistry() []OverrideSpec {
	registry := make([]OverrideSpec, len(overrideRegistry))
	copy(registry, overrideRegistry[:])
	return registry
}

// Overrides carries values supplied by command flags. Empty entries are unset.
type Overrides map[PathClass]string

// Source identifies the selecting precedence layer without carrying its value.
type Source string

const (
	SourceFlag            Source = "flag"
	SourceEnvironment     Source = "environment"
	SourcePlatformDefault Source = "platform-default"
)

// ResolvedPath is an absolute platform-bound path plus safe provenance.
type ResolvedPath struct {
	Value  scalar.AbsolutePath
	Source Source
}

// ResolvedPaths is an isolated process-lifetime path snapshot.
type ResolvedPaths struct {
	values map[PathClass]ResolvedPath
}

func (paths ResolvedPaths) Path(class PathClass) (ResolvedPath, bool) {
	value, ok := paths.values[class]
	return value, ok
}

func (paths ResolvedPaths) All() map[PathClass]ResolvedPath {
	values := make(map[PathClass]ResolvedPath, len(paths.values))
	for class, value := range paths.values {
		values[class] = value
	}
	return values
}

// Inputs captures all process inputs read during one resolution.
type Inputs struct {
	Platform   scalar.Platform
	HomeDir    string
	TempDir    string
	WorkingDir string
	LookupEnv  func(string) (string, bool)
	Stat       func(string) (fs.FileInfo, error)
	ReadFile   func(string) ([]byte, error)
}

// Snapshot contains one immutable path decision and selected TOML document.
type Snapshot struct {
	paths    ResolvedPaths
	document []byte
}

func (snapshot Snapshot) Paths() ResolvedPaths {
	return ResolvedPaths{values: snapshot.paths.All()}
}

func (snapshot Snapshot) Document() []byte {
	return append([]byte(nil), snapshot.document...)
}

// Error reports a failed class/layer without echoing machine-local values.
type Error struct {
	Operation string
	Class     PathClass
	Source    Source
	Err       error
}

func (err *Error) Error() string {
	if err.Class == "" {
		return fmt.Sprintf("configuration %s: %v", err.Operation, err.Err)
	}
	return fmt.Sprintf("configuration %s for %s from %s: %v", err.Operation, err.Class, err.Source, err.Err)
}

func (err *Error) Unwrap() error { return err.Err }

// OSInputs captures real process inputs once. The caller supplies the exact
// runtime-probed AX platform so WSL2 is never guessed from GOOS.
func OSInputs(platform scalar.Platform) (Inputs, error) {
	if _, err := scalar.ParsePlatform(platform.String()); err != nil {
		return Inputs{}, &Error{Operation: "capture OS inputs", Err: ErrInvalidContext}
	}
	home, err := os.UserHomeDir()
	if err != nil {
		return Inputs{}, &Error{Operation: "capture user home", Err: errors.Join(ErrInvalidContext, err)}
	}
	working, err := os.Getwd()
	if err != nil {
		return Inputs{}, &Error{Operation: "capture working directory", Err: errors.Join(ErrInvalidContext, err)}
	}
	return Inputs{
		Platform:   platform,
		HomeDir:    home,
		TempDir:    os.TempDir(),
		WorkingDir: working,
		LookupEnv:  os.LookupEnv,
		Stat:       os.Stat,
		ReadFile:   os.ReadFile,
	}, nil
}

func LoadOS(platform scalar.Platform, overrides Overrides) (Snapshot, error) {
	inputs, err := OSInputs(platform)
	if err != nil {
		return Snapshot{}, err
	}
	return Load(inputs, overrides)
}

// Load resolves all roots, then reads exactly the selected regular file.
func Load(inputs Inputs, overrides Overrides) (Snapshot, error) {
	paths, err := ResolvePaths(inputs, overrides)
	if err != nil {
		return Snapshot{}, err
	}
	if inputs.Stat == nil || inputs.ReadFile == nil {
		return Snapshot{}, &Error{Operation: "read selected file", Err: ErrInvalidContext}
	}
	if err := validateRootKinds(paths, inputs.Stat); err != nil {
		return Snapshot{}, err
	}

	selected, ok := paths.Path(ConfigFile)
	if !ok {
		return Snapshot{}, &Error{Operation: "read selected file", Class: ConfigFile, Err: ErrInvalidContext}
	}
	filename := selected.Value.String()
	info, err := inputs.Stat(filename)
	if err != nil {
		if errors.Is(err, fs.ErrNotExist) {
			return Snapshot{}, &Error{
				Operation: "stat selected file",
				Class:     ConfigFile,
				Source:    selected.Source,
				Err:       ErrConfigNotFound,
			}
		}
		return Snapshot{}, &Error{
			Operation: "stat selected file",
			Class:     ConfigFile,
			Source:    selected.Source,
			Err:       ErrConfigRead,
		}
	}
	if !info.Mode().IsRegular() {
		return Snapshot{}, &Error{
			Operation: "stat selected file",
			Class:     ConfigFile,
			Source:    selected.Source,
			Err:       ErrConfigNotRegular,
		}
	}

	document, err := inputs.ReadFile(filename)
	if err != nil {
		return Snapshot{}, &Error{
			Operation: "read selected file",
			Class:     ConfigFile,
			Source:    selected.Source,
			Err:       ErrConfigRead,
		}
	}
	return Snapshot{
		paths:    ResolvedPaths{values: paths.All()},
		document: append([]byte(nil), document...),
	}, nil
}

func validateRootKinds(paths ResolvedPaths, stat func(string) (fs.FileInfo, error)) error {
	for _, specification := range overrideRegistry {
		if specification.Class == ConfigFile {
			continue
		}
		resolved, ok := paths.Path(specification.Class)
		if !ok {
			return &Error{Operation: "inspect selected root", Class: specification.Class, Err: ErrInvalidContext}
		}
		info, err := stat(resolved.Value.String())
		if errors.Is(err, fs.ErrNotExist) {
			continue
		}
		if err != nil {
			return &Error{
				Operation: "inspect selected root",
				Class:     specification.Class,
				Source:    resolved.Source,
				Err:       ErrRootInspect,
			}
		}
		if !info.IsDir() {
			return &Error{
				Operation: "inspect selected root",
				Class:     specification.Class,
				Source:    resolved.Source,
				Err:       ErrRootNotDirectory,
			}
		}
	}
	return nil
}

// ResolvePaths applies flag, exact AX_* environment, then platform-default
// precedence for every registry member.
func ResolvePaths(inputs Inputs, overrides Overrides) (ResolvedPaths, error) {
	if _, err := scalar.ParsePlatform(inputs.Platform.String()); err != nil || inputs.LookupEnv == nil {
		return ResolvedPaths{}, &Error{Operation: "validate inputs", Err: ErrInvalidContext}
	}
	if err := validateOverrideClasses(overrides); err != nil {
		return ResolvedPaths{}, err
	}

	resolved := make(map[PathClass]ResolvedPath, len(overrideRegistry))
	for _, specification := range overrideRegistry {
		candidate, source, err := selectCandidate(inputs, overrides, specification)
		if err != nil {
			return ResolvedPaths{}, err
		}
		absolute, err := makeAbsolute(inputs.Platform, candidate, inputs.WorkingDir)
		if err != nil {
			return ResolvedPaths{}, &Error{
				Operation: "resolve absolute path",
				Class:     specification.Class,
				Source:    source,
				Err:       err,
			}
		}
		resolved[specification.Class] = ResolvedPath{Value: absolute, Source: source}
	}
	return ResolvedPaths{values: resolved}, nil
}

func validateOverrideClasses(overrides Overrides) error {
	known := make(map[PathClass]struct{}, len(overrideRegistry))
	for _, specification := range overrideRegistry {
		known[specification.Class] = struct{}{}
	}
	for class := range overrides {
		if _, ok := known[class]; !ok {
			return &Error{Operation: "validate override", Class: class, Source: SourceFlag, Err: ErrUnknownPathClass}
		}
	}
	return nil
}

func selectCandidate(inputs Inputs, overrides Overrides, specification OverrideSpec) (string, Source, error) {
	if value := overrides[specification.Class]; value != "" {
		return value, SourceFlag, nil
	}
	if value, ok := inputs.LookupEnv(specification.Environment); ok && value != "" {
		return value, SourceEnvironment, nil
	}
	value, err := platformDefault(inputs, specification.Class)
	if err != nil {
		return "", SourcePlatformDefault, &Error{
			Operation: "resolve platform default",
			Class:     specification.Class,
			Source:    SourcePlatformDefault,
			Err:       err,
		}
	}
	return value, SourcePlatformDefault, nil
}

func platformDefault(inputs Inputs, class PathClass) (string, error) {
	switch inputs.Platform {
	case scalar.PlatformMacOS:
		return macOSDefault(inputs, class)
	case scalar.PlatformLinux, scalar.PlatformWSL2:
		return linuxDefault(inputs, class)
	case scalar.PlatformWindows:
		return windowsDefault(inputs, class)
	default:
		return "", ErrInvalidContext
	}
}

func macOSDefault(inputs Inputs, class PathClass) (string, error) {
	switch class {
	case ConfigFile:
		base := nonEmptyEnvironment(inputs, "XDG_CONFIG_HOME")
		if base == "" {
			if inputs.HomeDir == "" {
				return "", ErrPlatformDefaultUnavailable
			}
			base = join(inputs.Platform, inputs.HomeDir, ".config")
		}
		return join(inputs.Platform, base, "ax", "config.toml"), nil
	case DataRoot:
		if inputs.HomeDir == "" {
			return "", ErrPlatformDefaultUnavailable
		}
		return join(inputs.Platform, inputs.HomeDir, "Library", "Application Support", "ax"), nil
	case StateRoot:
		if inputs.HomeDir == "" {
			return "", ErrPlatformDefaultUnavailable
		}
		return join(inputs.Platform, inputs.HomeDir, "Library", "Application Support", "ax", "state"), nil
	case CacheRoot:
		if inputs.HomeDir == "" {
			return "", ErrPlatformDefaultUnavailable
		}
		return join(inputs.Platform, inputs.HomeDir, "Library", "Caches", "ax"), nil
	case RuntimeRoot:
		if inputs.TempDir == "" {
			return "", ErrPlatformDefaultUnavailable
		}
		return join(inputs.Platform, inputs.TempDir, "ax"), nil
	default:
		return "", ErrUnknownPathClass
	}
}

func linuxDefault(inputs Inputs, class PathClass) (string, error) {
	var base string
	switch class {
	case ConfigFile:
		base = nonEmptyEnvironment(inputs, "XDG_CONFIG_HOME")
		if base == "" {
			if inputs.HomeDir == "" {
				return "", ErrPlatformDefaultUnavailable
			}
			base = join(inputs.Platform, inputs.HomeDir, ".config")
		}
		return join(inputs.Platform, base, "ax", "config.toml"), nil
	case DataRoot:
		base = nonEmptyEnvironment(inputs, "XDG_DATA_HOME")
		if base == "" {
			if inputs.HomeDir == "" {
				return "", ErrPlatformDefaultUnavailable
			}
			base = join(inputs.Platform, inputs.HomeDir, ".local", "share")
		}
	case StateRoot:
		base = nonEmptyEnvironment(inputs, "XDG_STATE_HOME")
		if base == "" {
			if inputs.HomeDir == "" {
				return "", ErrPlatformDefaultUnavailable
			}
			base = join(inputs.Platform, inputs.HomeDir, ".local", "state")
		}
	case CacheRoot:
		base = nonEmptyEnvironment(inputs, "XDG_CACHE_HOME")
		if base == "" {
			if inputs.HomeDir == "" {
				return "", ErrPlatformDefaultUnavailable
			}
			base = join(inputs.Platform, inputs.HomeDir, ".cache")
		}
	case RuntimeRoot:
		base = nonEmptyEnvironment(inputs, "XDG_RUNTIME_DIR")
		if base == "" {
			return "", ErrPlatformDefaultUnavailable
		}
	default:
		return "", ErrUnknownPathClass
	}
	return join(inputs.Platform, base, "ax"), nil
}

func windowsDefault(inputs Inputs, class PathClass) (string, error) {
	switch class {
	case ConfigFile:
		base := nonEmptyEnvironment(inputs, "APPDATA")
		if base == "" {
			return "", ErrPlatformDefaultUnavailable
		}
		return join(inputs.Platform, base, "ax", "config.toml"), nil
	case DataRoot, StateRoot, CacheRoot:
		base := nonEmptyEnvironment(inputs, "LOCALAPPDATA")
		if base == "" {
			return "", ErrPlatformDefaultUnavailable
		}
		leaf := map[PathClass]string{
			DataRoot:  "data",
			StateRoot: "state",
			CacheRoot: "cache",
		}[class]
		return join(inputs.Platform, base, "ax", leaf), nil
	case RuntimeRoot:
		if inputs.TempDir == "" {
			return "", ErrPlatformDefaultUnavailable
		}
		return join(inputs.Platform, inputs.TempDir, "ax"), nil
	default:
		return "", ErrUnknownPathClass
	}
}

func nonEmptyEnvironment(inputs Inputs, name string) string {
	value, ok := inputs.LookupEnv(name)
	if !ok || value == "" {
		return ""
	}
	return value
}

func join(platform scalar.Platform, elements ...string) string {
	if platform == scalar.PlatformWindows {
		return strings.Join(elements, "\\")
	}
	return path.Join(elements...)
}

func makeAbsolute(platform scalar.Platform, candidate, workingDirectory string) (scalar.AbsolutePath, error) {
	if candidate == "" {
		return scalar.AbsolutePath{}, ErrInvalidContext
	}
	var absolute string
	switch platform {
	case scalar.PlatformWindows:
		var err error
		absolute, err = absoluteWindowsPath(candidate, workingDirectory)
		if err != nil {
			return scalar.AbsolutePath{}, err
		}
	default:
		if strings.HasPrefix(candidate, "/") {
			absolute = path.Clean(candidate)
		} else {
			if !strings.HasPrefix(workingDirectory, "/") {
				return scalar.AbsolutePath{}, ErrInvalidContext
			}
			absolute = path.Join(workingDirectory, candidate)
		}
	}
	return scalar.ParseAbsolutePath(platform, absolute)
}

func absoluteWindowsPath(candidate, workingDirectory string) (string, error) {
	if strings.Contains(candidate, "/") || strings.Contains(workingDirectory, "/") {
		return "", ErrInvalidContext
	}
	if isWindowsAbsolute(candidate) {
		return cleanWindowsAbsolute(candidate)
	}
	if len(candidate) >= 2 && candidate[1] == ':' {
		return "", ErrInvalidContext
	}
	if !isWindowsAbsolute(workingDirectory) {
		return "", ErrInvalidContext
	}
	return cleanWindowsAbsolute(strings.TrimSuffix(workingDirectory, "\\") + "\\" + candidate)
}

func isWindowsAbsolute(value string) bool {
	return len(value) >= 3 && isASCIILetter(value[0]) && value[1] == ':' && value[2] == '\\' ||
		strings.HasPrefix(value, "\\\\")
}

func cleanWindowsAbsolute(value string) (string, error) {
	var prefix string
	var remainder string
	switch {
	case len(value) >= 3 && isASCIILetter(value[0]) && value[1] == ':' && value[2] == '\\':
		prefix = value[:3]
		remainder = value[3:]
	case strings.HasPrefix(value, "\\\\"):
		parts := strings.Split(value[2:], "\\")
		if len(parts) < 2 || parts[0] == "" || parts[1] == "" {
			return "", ErrInvalidContext
		}
		prefix = "\\\\" + parts[0] + "\\" + parts[1]
		remainder = strings.Join(parts[2:], "\\")
	default:
		return "", ErrInvalidContext
	}

	segments := make([]string, 0)
	for _, segment := range strings.Split(remainder, "\\") {
		switch segment {
		case "", ".":
			continue
		case "..":
			if len(segments) == 0 {
				return "", ErrInvalidContext
			}
			segments = segments[:len(segments)-1]
		default:
			segments = append(segments, segment)
		}
	}
	if len(segments) == 0 {
		if strings.HasPrefix(prefix, "\\\\") {
			return prefix, nil
		}
		return strings.TrimSuffix(prefix, "\\") + "\\", nil
	}
	return strings.TrimSuffix(prefix, "\\") + "\\" + strings.Join(segments, "\\"), nil
}

func isASCIILetter(value byte) bool {
	return value >= 'a' && value <= 'z' || value >= 'A' && value <= 'Z'
}

